// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 04-expressions/direct_call_local_argument_capability_neg_65.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A direct free-function call initializing a second local (`let y = g(v);`)
// is well-typed source the call lowering does not admit: the scalar-local
// carrier passes the owner local only as the sole argument of a returned call
// (`return g(v)`). The checker publishes the ordinary call fact, so the
// owning definition drains at the HIR capability gate as ZOM4099, never as an
// internal compiler error - the same rail the by-value aggregate init-result
// form uses.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/04-expressions/direct_call_local_argument_capability_neg_65.zom:4:1
